$\begin{align}
\blueE{10\%} \text{ of }\maroonD{60} &= \blueE{\dfrac{10}{100}} \cdot \maroonD{60}\\\\
&=\blueE{\dfrac{1}{10}} \cdot \maroonD{60}
\end{align}$

$\blueE{10\%}$ of a number *always* equals $\blueE{\dfrac{1}{10}}$ of the number.

What is $\blueE{\dfrac{1}{10}}$ of $\maroonD{60}$?
